WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.360
In our last high-speed video you saw Caesium, and it was really good

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:08.220
the way it reacted quite violently,

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:12.560
but then we thought we should have put an indicator in the water

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:17.860
To see what happened water. Did it go alkali as one might expect

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:20.480
and how fast as the indicator change?

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:24.280
So now we're going to show you rubidium

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:30.920
and in this experiment we put Phenolphthalein and indicate into the water

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:39.440
which has the advantage, it is colorless in mildly acidic water and pink if the water's okay.

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:55.440
It's quite complicated, what happened. So I want you to watch with me on my computer and I'll try and explain to what I can see

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:58.980
and then you can look at the videos and see what else you can see as well.

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:10.240
So what we've got here, and it's almost life-size because this is the actual... Umm... trough here but with no water in it.

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:17.260
We've got a trough of water and then ampoule with five grams, I think it was five grams, of rubidium here

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:24.400
It had almost melted by the time the experiment started and the hammer is just coming down here.

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:31.540
The hammer you remember is our so small metallic collider for breaking glass ampoules and here it's coming.

00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:34.460
and it hits the ampoule and breaks it

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:46.620
It is broken the ampoule about here above the metal

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:51.980
So there's a large lump of ampoule falling down with some rubidium inside it.

00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:55.600
Here, I put some metal things in to pretend it's rubidium,

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:59.920
and you can see it is hitting the water just about there,

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:04.240
and there's some tiny pieces of Rubidium coming down here

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:08.860
with white smoke trails because that's reacting with the water vapor in the air.

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:28.140
But what I think is exciting is that this whole trough

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:32.720
starts flexing around, and it's really hard to bend!

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:38.720
And even Brady who's tougher than me Can't bend it very much.

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:43.380
So and it's jumping about really very strongly

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:53.720
and now The reaction continues. There is a small piece of rubidium metal that is jumped out.

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:59.780
When the rubidium lands it hits some water and itself explodes on the ground

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:05.840
Now I should have explained that in front of this there was a plastic shield

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:14.060
So you will see bits of water hitting the shield, rather like the water hitting the windshield of a car.

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:32.420
Now the interesting thing is if you watch carefully there's another explosion.

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:38.380
So not just one, but the whole thing starts all over again

00:03:38.660 --> 00:03:46.260
and there's another eruption with the flexing of the Plastic Bowl

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:52.300
so what I think has happened is That when this Tube goes into the water

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:58.740
water rushes in and reacts with the rubidium producing explosively in amount of hydrogen

00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:05.300
and that this great rush of gas blows all the water out of the Tube so the reaction stops

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:11.940
and then the water goes back in again and you get another reaction and perhaps that happens two or three times

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:19.780
by luck Because we didn't smash the Tube at the bottom so all the metal got wet at the same time

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:25.820
we've got a repeat performance without having to have an action replay or whatever.

00:04:25.940 --> 00:04:28.560
So you get several reactions for the price of one.

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:34.820
So I'm just winding it back again because there's something else which you might have noticed

00:04:34.820 --> 00:04:38.000
but I only want noticed on the second or third time

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:46.500
So what you'll see in various points Is that there is a strong purple color or perhaps lilac might be better.

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:49.240
Which is actually the emission of light.

00:04:49.420 --> 00:04:52.440
from the vapor of the rubidium

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:56.340
in fact rubidium is well known to give this rather nice color

00:04:56.760 --> 00:05:02.520
and everything is getting so hot that you can see emissions here here and so on

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:09.260
of this light which is perhaps slightly masked by the pink color of the indicator

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:16.320
indicators like this one are acids which react with an alkali

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:19.600
and change their structure and change their color in

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:24.140
this particular case with phenolphthalein the acid is colorless

00:05:24.780 --> 00:05:28.400
and when you change structure it gets red

00:05:29.080 --> 00:05:30.980
Brady: Neil get cleaning mate

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:37.000
and the reason it goes red is that as the structure changes the energy levels of the electrons

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:42.460
within the molecule also change and so they absorb visible light

00:05:42.580 --> 00:05:48.760
and it looks red because in fact it's absorbing blue light so the red light can still get through

00:05:49.420 --> 00:05:54.360
and this reaction is very fast because what happens is that

00:05:55.220 --> 00:06:04.700
H+, and OH- ions are moving around very rapidly and they move through water at a very high speed

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:10.400
and so the reaction takes place very much faster than the speed of our camera

00:06:10.600 --> 00:06:17.640
the rubidium hydroxide is reacting with the acid

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:25.600
the colorless indicator to make rubidium phenolphthalate plus water

00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:33.020
so in effect H+ is leaving the acid and reacting with OH- to give water

